WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.530
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.614 --> 00:31.949
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.032 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:34.535 --> 00:35.786
[Wooju's mom] Elizabeth?

00:35.869 --> 00:37.246
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:37.329 --> 00:38.622
Elizabeth?

00:40.165 --> 00:45.087
Elizabeth. Elizabeth.

00:47.506 --> 00:48.632
Where did she go?

00:50.050 --> 00:51.051
[Elizabeth meows]

00:51.134 --> 00:52.427
[Wooju] Where is it?

00:54.388 --> 00:55.514
[sighing] Not here.

00:55.931 --> 00:57.724
[phone ringing]

00:57.808 --> 00:58.976
MOM

01:00.769 --> 01:01.853
ACCEPT

01:02.187 --> 01:04.273
-At Jenny's aunt's house?
-[Wooju] Yes.

01:04.356 --> 01:06.984
She'll be in Hong Kong until next month,
so she told me to take her there.

01:07.067 --> 01:09.778
You should've told me beforehand.
I was startled.

01:09.861 --> 01:11.738
Anyway, where is Jenny's aunt's house?

01:12.406 --> 01:13.615
Beauté Palace.

01:13.699 --> 01:15.158
Beauté Palace?

01:15.242 --> 01:17.703
Hey, I should've gone with you.

01:17.786 --> 01:19.830
Why would you come with me?

01:19.913 --> 01:21.623
What do you mean?

01:21.707 --> 01:23.500
I heard it's really exclusive.

01:23.584 --> 01:25.836
I could've looked around
and said hi while I was there.

01:25.919 --> 01:26.962
Should I head over now?

01:27.045 --> 01:28.463
No, I'm hanging up now.

01:28.547 --> 01:30.465
I'm leaving as soon as I drop her off.

01:31.049 --> 01:32.259
[line disconnects]

01:33.218 --> 01:35.470
[sighs] She has no idea how I feel.

01:37.681 --> 01:38.682
Where is it?

01:47.566 --> 01:49.109
[♪ dramatic music playing]

02:13.634 --> 02:15.927
That's not fair. I told you my wishes.

02:16.011 --> 02:18.597
-Don't ask.
-Then spit out the food you just ate.

02:19.514 --> 02:20.932
-[retching]
-[exclaims in disgust]

02:23.143 --> 02:24.478
Okay, then.

02:25.062 --> 02:26.438
Tell me if I catch you.

02:27.856 --> 02:29.149
[♪ dramatic sting]

02:31.610 --> 02:32.653
[Meri screams, gasps]

02:36.114 --> 02:37.532
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

02:37.616 --> 02:39.034
[slow, rhythmic heartbeats]

03:10.357 --> 03:11.441
[gasps softly]

03:16.363 --> 03:17.864
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

03:28.291 --> 03:29.418
[doorbell chimes]

03:29.501 --> 03:30.585
[sighs]

03:31.962 --> 03:33.880
-Who is that?
-Kim Wooju.

03:37.175 --> 03:38.218
[sighs]

03:39.261 --> 03:40.971
I swear that was Meri.

03:51.231 --> 03:52.607
Am I seeing things?

03:53.900 --> 03:54.943
[Elizabeth meows]

03:57.446 --> 03:58.738
-[meows]
-[exclaims worriedly]

03:58.822 --> 03:59.990
Elizabeth, stop!

04:00.073 --> 04:01.867
-Get back in there.
-[meows]

04:21.470 --> 04:22.804
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

04:33.690 --> 04:34.816
[sighs]

04:41.072 --> 04:42.240
Do you think he saw me?

04:43.116 --> 04:44.993
I'm sure he didn't.

04:45.076 --> 04:46.953
Either that, or he didn't recognize you.

04:47.704 --> 04:50.081
But didn't you say he was in Hong Kong?

04:50.832 --> 04:54.711
Actually, he called me to tell me
that he's back in Korea.

04:54.795 --> 04:57.047
But I hung up because I was flustered.

04:58.590 --> 05:00.050
Do you think he came here knowingly?

05:00.133 --> 05:02.219
Well, then he wouldn't have just left.

05:04.888 --> 05:06.223
You're right. He wouldn't.

05:06.306 --> 05:09.768
But if in the worst case...

05:12.896 --> 05:14.147
The worst case?

05:14.648 --> 05:16.066
If he came knowing everything,

05:16.149 --> 05:20.028
then we can only tell the truth
and team up with him.

05:20.111 --> 05:21.279
No way.

05:22.113 --> 05:24.616
It's unlikely
that he'll give up on this house.

05:24.699 --> 05:26.535
That means he won't easily expose us.

05:27.035 --> 05:29.412
And since you two
are still legally married,

05:29.496 --> 05:31.081
Beauté won't cancel your winning.

05:35.418 --> 05:37.712
I'd rather get caught

05:37.796 --> 05:40.257
than team up with Wooju.

05:40.924 --> 05:43.802
Not after what he and his family did
to me and my mom.

05:44.845 --> 05:46.471
If he knew that I won this,

05:46.555 --> 05:48.849
he'd gleefully threaten me with it.

05:48.932 --> 05:52.060
It's obvious that he'll demand this house
in exchange for keeping the secret.

05:52.143 --> 05:53.353
I can't bear to see that.

05:53.436 --> 05:54.437
[sighs]

05:54.521 --> 05:58.024
I get that you're feeling wronged,
but what about the loan?

05:58.108 --> 06:01.027
Isn't the money you borrowed
from your mom everything she had?

06:01.444 --> 06:02.821
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

06:02.904 --> 06:07.200
The person who needs this house
more than anyone is you, not him.

06:08.702 --> 06:13.373
So, don't get emotional
and just think rationally.

06:16.877 --> 06:19.129
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

06:19.212 --> 06:20.213
EPISODE 6

06:20.297 --> 06:21.298
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

06:21.381 --> 06:23.884
[fitness trainer] One, two, three, four.

06:23.967 --> 06:25.594
The other side.

06:25.677 --> 06:26.887
Left foot behind.

06:26.970 --> 06:31.224
Going low. One, two, three.

06:31.308 --> 06:33.143
Let's stretch our hips. One.

06:33.894 --> 06:35.020
The other side. Two.

06:35.687 --> 06:36.771
Three.

06:37.480 --> 06:40.859
After a five-minute break,
we'll lightly stretch and start.

06:40.942 --> 06:42.944
Okay, let's all give a round of applause.

06:43.028 --> 06:45.196
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

06:49.826 --> 06:51.453
You got new trainers.

06:51.536 --> 06:53.246
You noticed already. [chuckles]

06:53.788 --> 06:56.333
I told you that my feet hurt
if I run for a long time.

06:56.416 --> 06:58.918
Apparently, it's because
my arches collapsed.

06:59.002 --> 07:02.881
So, I had my feet scanned
and got custom trainers.

07:02.964 --> 07:04.466
I could fly away in these.

07:04.549 --> 07:07.469
-I guess exercise is all about the gear.
-Yes, it is.

07:07.552 --> 07:10.180
You should try
for a half-marathon this time, then.

07:10.263 --> 07:12.932
I was also thinking of trying out for it.

07:13.767 --> 07:14.809
[exclaims softly]

07:15.101 --> 07:16.102
He shows up regularly.

07:16.811 --> 07:17.979
[chuckles softly]

07:19.606 --> 07:21.024
He is the managing director.

07:22.359 --> 07:24.653
He's a true young-and-rich
who lives in Beauté Palace.

07:25.612 --> 07:28.156
Apparently, he's the reason Beauté hit

07:28.239 --> 07:30.200
legendary sales numbers
three years in a row.

07:30.784 --> 07:32.160
Isn't he so dashing?

07:32.243 --> 07:33.870
I guess he's good at his job.

07:33.953 --> 07:35.705
But he's so cold and unapproachable.

07:36.289 --> 07:38.583
He doesn't even stay for a beer afterward.

07:39.751 --> 07:41.169
I think he's single, though.

07:41.670 --> 07:43.171
Let him be. He seems busy.

07:43.254 --> 07:44.923
[fitness trainer] Okay, let's get started.

07:45.006 --> 07:47.467
If you don't feel well,
let me know straight away.

07:47.550 --> 07:48.885
Keep your pace in check.

07:48.968 --> 07:50.720
Also, keep your distance.

07:50.804 --> 07:52.472
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

07:59.396 --> 08:02.273
-[fitness trainer] Let's go.
-Yeah, let's go!

08:02.357 --> 08:03.858
[taking deep breaths]

08:15.829 --> 08:16.913
[♪ foreboding music playing]

08:16.996 --> 08:18.039
[groans]

08:19.916 --> 08:21.459
-[groans]
-[woman] Ma'am!

08:21.543 --> 08:22.627
Are you okay?

08:22.711 --> 08:23.795
-Stop!
-Hold!

08:23.878 --> 08:25.130
-Ma'am!
-Can you hear me?

08:25.213 --> 08:27.090
[woman] Oh, my gosh!

08:28.508 --> 08:29.759
Does anyone have their phone?

08:29.843 --> 08:31.511
-Hey...
-What's wrong?

08:31.594 --> 08:33.054
[Jingyeong] Excuse me.

08:33.138 --> 08:34.180
[panting]

08:36.057 --> 08:38.101
Ma'am, are you okay?

08:38.184 --> 08:39.477
Can you hear me?

08:39.561 --> 08:40.729
[continues panting]

08:44.149 --> 08:46.651
Call 911 and tell them
that someone's in cardiac arrest.

08:46.735 --> 08:47.944
-Okay.
-[line connects]

08:48.028 --> 08:51.156
We're at Hangang River Park,
and we have a medical emergency.

08:51.614 --> 08:53.366
We're currently at... Please hold.

08:53.450 --> 08:55.410
Check if there's an AED
at the information center.

08:55.493 --> 08:56.870
I'll go get it.

08:56.953 --> 08:58.246
[breathing heavily]

09:05.545 --> 09:06.963
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

09:08.673 --> 09:09.674
[gasps softly]

09:10.050 --> 09:11.051
[panting]

09:15.513 --> 09:17.223
[camera shutter clicking]

09:17.766 --> 09:19.517
Stop recording and let's go.

09:19.601 --> 09:20.894
Why? This is great.

09:20.977 --> 09:23.396
-We'll be in trouble if we get caught.
-Give me a break.

09:25.440 --> 09:26.816
[Jingyeong] Oh, no.

09:26.900 --> 09:28.068
[panting]

09:34.157 --> 09:35.325
[camera shutter clicks]

09:42.165 --> 09:43.500
[Sanghyeon] Let me take over.

09:47.212 --> 09:49.422
[Jingyeong] Excuse me, what are you doing?

09:49.506 --> 09:52.175
-Do you even know how?
-You should cover yourself up.

09:52.675 --> 09:53.968
[♪ pop-rock music playing]

10:09.067 --> 10:12.195
I think this one will tip over
when we pull out the drawer

10:12.278 --> 10:14.405
from the weight of the hangwa.

10:14.489 --> 10:15.573
[sharp inhale]

10:15.657 --> 10:17.492
Side-opening drawers would be better.

10:17.992 --> 10:21.538
I think so, too.
It would showcase the items better.

10:21.621 --> 10:22.622
[acknowledges]

10:23.456 --> 10:25.166
But this part looks a little dull.

10:25.250 --> 10:27.085
It might be nice to add
an accent to the handles.

10:27.794 --> 10:29.712
How about fancy gold leaf detailing?

10:29.796 --> 10:31.214
No.

10:31.297 --> 10:34.467
Let's focus on the design,
not the materials.

10:34.551 --> 10:39.305
A sleek linear or round design
would maintain that elegant simplicity.

10:40.515 --> 10:43.101
I'll come up
with more designs for the handle.

10:43.184 --> 10:45.186
Could you contact Monk Haeho, Songhee?

10:45.270 --> 10:46.437
Okay.

10:55.446 --> 10:56.531
[♪ feel-good music playing]

10:56.614 --> 10:59.534
[Meri] We've set the packaging concept
as "jewelry box."

11:00.743 --> 11:03.496
It symbolizes a jewelry box
containing hangwa

11:03.580 --> 11:05.498
that's as precious
and beautiful as jewels.

11:05.582 --> 11:09.460
If we're allowed to make it function
like an actual jewelry box afterward,

11:09.544 --> 11:11.671
it will be made of wood rather than paper.

11:14.215 --> 11:16.301
Wouldn't the costs spike?

11:16.759 --> 11:19.554
Specialty paper
isn't exactly cheap, either.

11:19.637 --> 11:23.933
I got separate quotes for paper, wood,
and mother-of-pearl options.

11:24.017 --> 11:27.061
[inhales sharply] I think mother-of-pearl
would cater to specific preferences.

11:27.145 --> 11:28.271
And it might seem outdated.

11:28.354 --> 11:30.148
I also think wood would be better.

11:30.231 --> 11:32.567
We have a few VVIPs in their 20s and 30s.

11:32.650 --> 11:35.069
-Right.
-[Kim Wooju] Let's settle with wood, then.

11:35.570 --> 11:37.071
And we'll adjust the cost accordingly.

11:37.155 --> 11:39.365
[sharp inhale]
How's the thank-you card going?

11:39.490 --> 11:44.162
We're planning to incorporate a verse
from Monk Haeho's poetry.

11:44.245 --> 11:45.914
He's famous for his calligraphy.

11:45.997 --> 11:47.790
Who is Monk Haeho? Is he famous?

11:47.874 --> 11:49.292
Yes, he's trending these days.

11:49.375 --> 11:51.002
He's also famous for couples counseling.

11:51.085 --> 11:52.170
-True.
-[Ms. Oh] Really?

11:52.253 --> 11:54.797
-Did you get his approval?
-[Meri] Yes, we did.

11:54.881 --> 11:57.800
We're currently deciding
which poem to calligraph.

12:03.389 --> 12:05.225
[bystander] What happened?

12:06.434 --> 12:08.603
-I performed CPR for about seven minutes.
-Okay.

12:08.686 --> 12:10.855
-The patient is conscious now.
-Got it.

12:10.939 --> 12:12.565
We'll transport the patient now.

12:14.692 --> 12:15.818
[siren wailing]

12:18.238 --> 12:19.239
[sighs in relief]

12:19.322 --> 12:20.531
[indistinct chatter]

12:30.875 --> 12:32.043
[♪ rock music playing]

12:34.087 --> 12:35.088
[both grunt]

12:35.797 --> 12:36.798
[grunts]

12:37.757 --> 12:38.841
[groans]

12:43.930 --> 12:44.931
[grunts]

12:45.223 --> 12:46.307
[screams]

12:46.766 --> 12:48.434
Wait...

12:48.977 --> 12:50.061
[groans]

12:51.354 --> 12:52.689
-Passcode.
-[panting]

12:53.940 --> 12:55.984
[screams] It's 0901.

12:57.819 --> 12:59.862
Illegal filming carries
up to seven years in prison

12:59.946 --> 13:01.239
and a 50-million-won fine.

13:01.322 --> 13:03.116
If forensics reveals more,

13:03.950 --> 13:06.160
you'll be charged
as a repeat offender with no leniency.

13:07.745 --> 13:09.205
If you are a repeat offender,

13:10.081 --> 13:13.042
even rich parents will have
a hard time getting you out.

13:13.126 --> 13:14.335
[exclaims in pain] Damn it.

13:14.836 --> 13:16.671
He made me do it.

13:16.754 --> 13:17.755
I did not.

13:17.839 --> 13:19.841
Hey, you made me do it.

13:19.924 --> 13:21.926
You threatened me if I didn't record it.

13:30.810 --> 13:32.103
MOVE TO TRASH

13:33.646 --> 13:36.274
I'll let you off
since it looks like your first time.

13:36.357 --> 13:37.734
But I won't the next time.

13:38.568 --> 13:39.652
[phone clatters]

13:39.736 --> 13:40.778
[panting]

13:48.870 --> 13:49.871
Hey.

13:55.418 --> 13:56.419
Come here.

14:11.601 --> 14:12.810
Do you get good grades?

14:13.770 --> 14:14.771
Pardon?

14:17.398 --> 14:18.399
I do.

14:18.900 --> 14:20.151
You'll have to be really smart

14:21.194 --> 14:24.113
if you want to pick up the crumbs
next to your rich friend.

14:24.530 --> 14:25.990
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

14:28.034 --> 14:29.035
[clicks tongue]

14:33.206 --> 14:35.208
[train approaching, rumbles past]

14:40.755 --> 14:42.256
Okay, got it.

14:43.800 --> 14:44.801
[line disconnects]

14:44.884 --> 14:45.885
Beauté confirmed.

14:45.968 --> 14:46.969
[gasps]

14:47.053 --> 14:49.055
-It passed on the first try!
-Oh, yes!

14:49.430 --> 14:50.765
Good work.

14:50.848 --> 14:53.184
No, you did all the work.

14:53.267 --> 14:54.519
-Listen to you.
-[phone vibrating]

14:54.602 --> 14:56.604
Your social skills have come a long way.

14:56.938 --> 14:59.440
[chuckles softly] I could send you out
for sales now.

15:01.484 --> 15:02.527
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU

15:02.610 --> 15:04.737
[Kim Wooju] I loved your packaging idea.

15:04.821 --> 15:06.572
It shows you put a lot of thought into it.

15:07.031 --> 15:09.367
[Meri] I'm glad that I could be of help.

15:09.450 --> 15:10.827
[♪ whimsical music playing]

15:16.124 --> 15:18.334
-Is it your boyfriend?
-No.

15:19.293 --> 15:22.130
You were smiling
from ear to ear while texting.

15:22.213 --> 15:23.256
Nonsense.

15:23.339 --> 15:24.841
How's your wedding preparation going?

15:24.924 --> 15:25.925
What?

15:26.008 --> 15:27.135
[chuckles, gasps]

15:28.219 --> 15:29.220
[Songhee chuckles softly]

15:30.221 --> 15:31.472
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

15:31.556 --> 15:33.516
[Songhee] Speak of the devil.

15:34.225 --> 15:36.978
Looks like he missed you already
and came running.

15:38.771 --> 15:39.772
Hello.

15:40.606 --> 15:41.607
Hi.

15:45.570 --> 15:47.196
[♪ dramatic sting]

16:00.334 --> 16:03.421
And if Wooju contacts you again,

16:03.504 --> 16:06.048
we'll need to find out his motives.

16:10.428 --> 16:11.429
What brings you here?

16:15.433 --> 16:16.559
I just wanted to see you.

16:19.020 --> 16:22.064
[chuckles] Gosh, it's been a while
since I've been here.

16:22.148 --> 16:23.858
Was it three years ago?

16:23.941 --> 16:26.903
You got fired
and rented this place to go independent.

16:26.986 --> 16:29.947
For the opening ritual,
we got boiled pork slices, Choco Pies,

16:30.031 --> 16:31.949
and makgeolli from the convenience store.

16:33.159 --> 16:34.243
Do you remember?

16:38.831 --> 16:42.001
After the ritual and sending Songhee home,

16:43.044 --> 16:44.462
do you remember what we did?

16:47.298 --> 16:49.258
-We kissed--
-Where are you getting at?

16:50.843 --> 16:51.886
[chuckles sheepishly]

16:52.261 --> 16:53.721
Nowhere, I was just reminiscing.

16:58.559 --> 17:00.811
Oh, what did you do on Sunday?

17:00.895 --> 17:01.896
[♪ dramatic music playing]

17:01.979 --> 17:02.980
Why do you ask?

17:03.064 --> 17:05.024
My friend's acquaintance lives
at Beauté Palace,

17:05.107 --> 17:08.236
so I went there for something,
and saw someone who looked just like you.

17:09.195 --> 17:11.489
I was just wondering if it really was you.

17:14.325 --> 17:18.579
I was in the office the whole weekend.

17:18.663 --> 17:19.789
I have a lot to do these days.

17:19.872 --> 17:21.207
Right?

17:21.290 --> 17:23.584
Of course, there's no way you'd be there.

17:23.668 --> 17:25.044
That's what I thought.

17:25.127 --> 17:26.420
You must've been mistaken.

17:28.297 --> 17:30.258
That's how I am these days.

17:30.341 --> 17:31.509
I'm seeing things now.

17:32.510 --> 17:35.054
It might be because you're
on my mind day and night.

17:35.346 --> 17:37.014
-[scoffs softly]
-These days...

17:39.767 --> 17:41.018
I think a lot about you.

17:41.102 --> 17:42.311
[sighs]

17:43.646 --> 17:45.273
Does your new girlfriend know

17:46.774 --> 17:48.150
that you're acting like this?

17:48.234 --> 17:49.277
I broke up with Jenny.

17:50.903 --> 17:52.488
I understand her position.

17:52.572 --> 17:54.156
She knew I wasn't over you.

17:54.740 --> 17:56.867
She told me to make a choice.

17:57.618 --> 17:58.619
And my choice...

18:01.038 --> 18:02.039
was you, Meri.

18:03.165 --> 18:04.917
[chuckles] Honestly...

18:05.001 --> 18:06.919
I just couldn't get over you.

18:07.003 --> 18:09.338
That's why I called
as soon as I came back to Seoul.

18:15.386 --> 18:16.971
Since we're on the subject,

18:18.514 --> 18:20.057
I want us to get back together.

18:21.309 --> 18:22.893
Like you generously used to,

18:24.228 --> 18:26.188
could you forgive my momentary mistake?

18:26.272 --> 18:27.315
I'm sorry,

18:27.815 --> 18:28.899
but do I have to?

18:30.484 --> 18:32.486
You were like this every time we argued.

18:32.945 --> 18:34.322
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

18:34.405 --> 18:36.699
And I understood
and forgave you every time.

18:36.782 --> 18:39.076
I thought that's what you do
when you love someone.

18:39.535 --> 18:40.661
But not anymore.

18:41.787 --> 18:45.291
It's not because of your mom,
who has always been embarrassed by me.

18:45.374 --> 18:46.834
It's also not because of you.

18:48.336 --> 18:50.046
It's because my mindset changed.

18:50.921 --> 18:52.256
How can love change?

18:52.340 --> 18:53.507
It did for me

18:54.675 --> 18:56.427
because I was hurt too many times.

18:58.429 --> 19:00.973
Is this because I didn't
answer your call in Hong Kong?

19:01.057 --> 19:03.643
-Back then, I was--
-Yes, I think it started then.

19:03.726 --> 19:07.897
I want to be with someone
who's there for me when I'm struggling.

19:07.980 --> 19:10.358
Not someone who wants me
only when they need me.

19:13.527 --> 19:14.528
Meri.

19:17.114 --> 19:19.116
[sighs] This conversation itself
is ridiculous.

19:19.200 --> 19:20.576
It's already over between us.

19:21.118 --> 19:23.287
Can you leave now? I need to work.

19:23.913 --> 19:24.914
What?

19:26.832 --> 19:27.958
Oh, sure.

19:28.459 --> 19:30.670
I guess you're a bit emotional right now.

19:30.753 --> 19:33.005
Let's talk again later.

19:50.981 --> 19:52.066
[door closes]

19:52.149 --> 19:53.943
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

19:54.026 --> 19:55.111
[sighs]

20:00.074 --> 20:01.158
[sighs wearily]

20:22.430 --> 20:23.889
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

20:34.608 --> 20:36.944
I'VE PLANTED YOU LIKE A FLOWER IN MY HEART

20:37.027 --> 20:38.112
CEO YOO MERI

20:42.241 --> 20:43.367
[mouse clicking]

20:47.955 --> 20:49.415
[die-cut machine clicks rhythmically]

21:14.356 --> 21:15.441
Name?

21:16.108 --> 21:17.443
[continues indistinctly]

21:23.574 --> 21:24.992
HANGIL DELIVERY EXPRESS

21:41.967 --> 21:44.053
MARKETING TEAM

21:44.512 --> 21:45.679
-What?
-[♪ dramatic sting]

21:45.763 --> 21:46.889
What's this?

21:47.431 --> 21:48.516
Mr. Han.

21:48.599 --> 21:50.601
Ms. Oh, Mr. Kim,
I think you need to see this.

21:52.436 --> 21:54.146
-What is it?
-[Wonseok] What?

21:59.151 --> 22:00.361
DRUNK PASSENGER DISRUPTS FLIGHT

22:02.238 --> 22:04.740
ASSAULTING CREW AND IN-FLIGHT DISTURBANCES

22:04.824 --> 22:06.450
THE FAMOUS MONK HAEHO DISRUPTED A FLIGHT

22:06.534 --> 22:07.535
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

22:07.618 --> 22:10.788
Monk Haeho,
famous as a poet and life coach,

22:11.163 --> 22:13.415
was arrested by the airport police

22:13.499 --> 22:15.292
after causing
a drunken disturbance on a flight.

22:15.835 --> 22:18.671
On yesterday's 7:00 p.m. flight
from Incheon International Airport

22:18.754 --> 22:22.550
to J.FC International Airport in New York,

22:22.967 --> 22:25.135
video footage has emerged
showing disruptive behavior

22:25.219 --> 22:28.097
and assault on the flight crew,
sparking public outrage.

22:28.806 --> 22:32.560
The individual in the video
has been identified as Monk Haeho,

22:32.643 --> 22:34.979
a public figure who has been active
as a poet and life coach,

22:35.271 --> 22:36.689
using his influence for good...

22:36.772 --> 22:38.065
[sighs wearily]

22:38.148 --> 22:40.609
Our calligraphy is doomed.

22:40.693 --> 22:41.694
What do we do?

22:41.777 --> 22:43.279
Haven't we finished that already?

22:43.362 --> 22:44.780
Are the deliveries complete?

22:44.864 --> 22:46.907
-When are they delivering?
-Today.

22:46.991 --> 22:49.368
Can you check
if the deliveries have begun?

22:50.828 --> 22:51.871
[Ms. Oh sighs]

22:53.289 --> 22:54.582
[Miyeon sighs softly]

22:55.374 --> 22:57.751
That's not a big deal.

22:58.335 --> 23:00.337
We can just take out the cards.

23:00.421 --> 23:03.132
The issue is that the deliveries
have already begun.

23:03.799 --> 23:05.509
I just went to check
on the marketing team.

23:05.593 --> 23:06.802
It's like someone died in there.

23:06.886 --> 23:11.056
Beauté is calling
to complain and everything.

23:11.140 --> 23:13.893
If Grandma finds out,
Wooju might get fired.

23:13.976 --> 23:15.394
It's that serious, Mom.

23:15.477 --> 23:16.937
Calls from Beauté?

23:17.021 --> 23:18.022
That's not good.

23:18.105 --> 23:19.273
What are you saying?

23:19.356 --> 23:22.109
With Wooju gone,
I can go back to the marketing team.

23:22.192 --> 23:24.153
Hey!

23:25.279 --> 23:28.824
That deal's happening because your dad
has connections with Beauté's CEO.

23:28.908 --> 23:31.076
We can't mess it up.

23:32.077 --> 23:33.078
[inaudible]

23:33.162 --> 23:34.705
This could blow back on your dad.

23:35.414 --> 23:36.415
[clicks tongue]

23:36.498 --> 23:40.502
Gosh, Wooju acts so smart,
yet how can he mess up like this?

23:40.586 --> 23:41.754
Embarrassing his uncle...

23:41.837 --> 23:44.173
Honestly, he's useless.

23:44.256 --> 23:45.925
-Hey, Mom.
-What?

23:46.008 --> 23:49.094
Who will you save
if Dad and I fall in the water?

23:49.178 --> 23:50.804
What kind of ridiculous question is that?

23:50.888 --> 23:52.014
Are you hungry or something?

23:52.139 --> 23:55.476
No, but I think
you'll choose your husband over your son.

23:55.559 --> 23:57.895
You think I should save you?

23:57.978 --> 23:59.730
We already taught you how to swim.

23:59.813 --> 24:03.025
You were taught by the national athlete.
You should swim on your own.

24:03.108 --> 24:05.110
On the other hand, your dad can't swim.

24:05.194 --> 24:07.071
And he only knows me.

24:07.154 --> 24:09.198
Even when I was getting married,

24:09.281 --> 24:12.534
he caused a scene in front of my dad,
saying he couldn't live without me.

24:12.618 --> 24:16.830
I married him,
thinking that it was like saving his life.

24:16.914 --> 24:17.957
[snickers]

24:18.040 --> 24:20.542
Mom, let's not distort history.

24:20.626 --> 24:25.255
Everyone knows
that you were begging him to marry you.

24:25.339 --> 24:29.051
Anyway, Mom, you need to depend on
and trust me, not Dad.

24:29.134 --> 24:32.554
When you get old,
I'll be the one next to you.

24:32.638 --> 24:34.848
Gosh, how creepy.

24:35.849 --> 24:37.267
Thank you.

24:37.351 --> 24:38.894
I'm sorry to bother you like this.

24:39.979 --> 24:41.563
-What did they say?
-Well, for now,

24:41.647 --> 24:44.149
they've put a hold on all delivery men
that they could contact.

24:44.233 --> 24:46.568
But apparently, they can't get in touch
with a few of them.

24:46.652 --> 24:49.530
Texts have been sent,
but it seems they aren't checking them.

24:49.613 --> 24:51.907
It's hard to look at the phone
during deliveries.

24:53.993 --> 24:54.994
We should go.

24:55.077 --> 24:56.453
-Pardon?
-Now?

24:56.870 --> 24:58.664
-Us?
-It's doable

24:58.747 --> 25:00.541
if we split by region
and catch up with the trucks.

25:01.041 --> 25:04.378
It's only been an hour since they left,
so we'll catch up if we leave now.

25:04.461 --> 25:06.672
-We just remove the cards, right?
-Yes.

25:06.755 --> 25:08.674
Sejung, give us the delivery addresses.

25:08.757 --> 25:09.758
Okay.

25:09.842 --> 25:11.510
[♪ enthralling music playing]

25:12.011 --> 25:13.012
Ms. Oh.

25:13.095 --> 25:14.763
Here's yours, Mr. Kim.

25:15.389 --> 25:17.182
How are we supposed to do this?

25:18.142 --> 25:20.019
-[Ms. Oh] Where is Ms. Yoo?
-I'm right here.

25:20.102 --> 25:21.520
[Ms. Oh] Ms. Yoo!

25:21.603 --> 25:23.897
How could you let this happen?

25:23.981 --> 25:24.982
I'm sorry.

25:25.065 --> 25:26.692
This isn't Ms. Yoo's fault.

25:27.818 --> 25:29.570
-Shall we get going then?
-Okay.

25:32.656 --> 25:33.866
Come with me, Songhee.

25:35.409 --> 25:37.703
Sejung, you come with me.
I'll go get ready.

25:37.786 --> 25:38.787
[Sejung] Us together?

25:42.791 --> 25:44.710
DELIVERY ADDRESS LIST

25:44.793 --> 25:46.086
[line ringing]

25:47.671 --> 25:48.756
[line connects]

25:48.839 --> 25:50.049
Sir!

25:50.132 --> 25:51.842
I'm calling from Myungsoondang.

25:51.925 --> 25:54.219
-You're out on delivery, right?
-Ask him where he is.

25:54.303 --> 25:55.554
Where about are you?

25:57.639 --> 25:59.058
-Yongsan?
-Tell him we're coming.

25:59.141 --> 26:01.852
We're on our way now.
There's a mix-up in the orders, sir.

26:02.478 --> 26:03.479
Yes.

26:03.562 --> 26:05.272
Yes, okay.

26:05.814 --> 26:07.858
Thank you so much!

26:08.984 --> 26:10.778
What a relief.

26:10.861 --> 26:14.114
He couldn't start the deliveries yet
due to the traffic.

26:14.198 --> 26:15.866
Let's go to Yongsan Park!

26:15.949 --> 26:17.242
[motorbike engine roars]

26:17.326 --> 26:18.869
[♪ dramatic rock music playing]

26:29.546 --> 26:30.547
Here.

26:32.132 --> 26:34.259
I think taking the taxi would be faster.

26:34.343 --> 26:36.804
This is the best
if we are using shortcuts.

26:36.887 --> 26:40.349
Mr. Han, when did you start
biking to work?

26:40.432 --> 26:42.601
Me? I do this from time to time.

26:43.352 --> 26:45.145
-Haven't you seen me?
-You have a license, right?

26:45.729 --> 26:47.731
Geez, my family owns a Chinese restaurant,

26:47.815 --> 26:49.775
so I've been riding one
since middle school.

26:49.858 --> 26:51.777
Hop on already. Come this way.

26:54.404 --> 26:55.405
Good.

26:56.073 --> 26:57.074
Okay.

26:57.533 --> 26:58.951
Here we go. Hold on tight.

26:59.034 --> 27:00.160
[engine revs]

27:01.745 --> 27:02.746
[Sejung screams]

27:08.877 --> 27:10.170
HANGIL DELIVERY
EXPRESS

27:17.928 --> 27:19.012
[tires screech]

27:20.097 --> 27:21.181
[delivery agent] Gosh.

27:22.432 --> 27:23.559
-Sir.
-Sir!

27:33.527 --> 27:34.570
[chuckling awkwardly]

27:37.364 --> 27:38.490
[both gasp]

27:38.782 --> 27:39.783
[Wonseok] Give it to me.

27:41.201 --> 27:42.244
[sighs]

27:43.120 --> 27:44.162
I'm really sorry.

27:44.246 --> 27:45.998
This was really important.

27:46.081 --> 27:47.541
Oh, I see.

27:51.295 --> 27:52.713
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

27:53.213 --> 27:55.382
Mr. Han, is this how you do this?

27:55.465 --> 27:57.885
Gosh, don't make it crooked.

27:57.968 --> 28:00.679
-They'll notice that it's been undone.
-Oh, how do you tie this?

28:00.762 --> 28:02.723
Let me. Give it here.

28:04.266 --> 28:06.101
You go like this.

28:07.769 --> 28:09.897
And if you go like this...

28:09.980 --> 28:11.106
[chuckles nervously]

28:11.607 --> 28:12.941
It looks weird.

28:13.025 --> 28:14.610
I told you.

28:14.693 --> 28:16.904
Sejung, should we call Ms. Yoo?

28:17.779 --> 28:18.864
[Meri] Hold both ends.

28:20.449 --> 28:21.617
And tie it once.

28:21.700 --> 28:23.368
[♪ feel-good music playing]

28:23.452 --> 28:25.454
Create a hook with your left hand.

28:26.705 --> 28:30.000
-No, this part has to be on the outside.
-[Wonseok] Oh, I see.

28:31.126 --> 28:32.419
Like this?

28:32.502 --> 28:33.503
Yes, that's right.

28:33.587 --> 28:39.051
Put this end through the hook
to complete the knot.

28:39.134 --> 28:40.510
And lastly,

28:41.303 --> 28:43.972
just tidy up this middle part
so that it's pretty.

28:45.599 --> 28:47.309
-I did it!
-It worked!

28:47.392 --> 28:49.311
-We did it!
-[Meri] Good.

28:51.813 --> 28:53.732
Oh, where is Mr. Kim?

28:54.358 --> 28:55.484
I thought you went with him.

28:57.361 --> 28:59.571
I'm waiting for the deliveryman here.

28:59.655 --> 29:04.326
Mr. Kim went to get the package
that had already been delivered nearby.

29:11.333 --> 29:12.542
[mumbles]

29:24.221 --> 29:25.263
[sighs]

29:27.265 --> 29:28.600
-Okay.
-[dog barking]

29:29.476 --> 29:30.560
What?

29:31.687 --> 29:33.605
[in English] Calm down.

29:33.689 --> 29:35.148
-[in Korean] Good boy.
-[growling]

29:35.232 --> 29:37.693
-I wasn't trying to steal this.
-[barking]

29:39.444 --> 29:40.862
I'll just put it back, okay?

29:41.697 --> 29:43.156
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

29:45.242 --> 29:46.243
Hey!

29:46.743 --> 29:47.911
[continues barking]

29:59.297 --> 30:01.174
[♪ dramatic sting]

30:04.386 --> 30:05.470
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

30:09.558 --> 30:10.934
Okay, sit.

30:11.476 --> 30:12.686
Good boy.

30:12.769 --> 30:13.937
Wait.

30:14.021 --> 30:15.272
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

30:17.065 --> 30:18.400
Such a good boy.

30:18.483 --> 30:19.484
Sit.

30:19.568 --> 30:20.777
Good. Now, wait.

30:21.653 --> 30:22.654
[chuckles]

30:22.863 --> 30:24.031
Wait. [chuckles]

30:25.073 --> 30:26.575
I'm so sorry.

30:26.658 --> 30:29.286
His leash slipped out of my hand
while I was parking.

30:29.411 --> 30:30.454
[acknowledges]

30:30.537 --> 30:31.580
No, it's okay.

30:31.663 --> 30:33.957
I'm really sorry.

30:34.666 --> 30:36.501
-Let's go, baby.
-Bye.

30:38.128 --> 30:40.130
He is so lucky.

30:40.213 --> 30:41.631
I was just about to knock him over.

30:41.715 --> 30:43.258
-[♪ whimsical music playing]
-[giggles]

30:43.341 --> 30:44.342
Why do you laugh?

30:44.801 --> 30:46.303
Nothing. Let's go.

30:46.762 --> 30:48.096
-[giggles]
-[exclaims quizzically]

30:50.432 --> 30:53.268
-[clears throat]
-Anyway, where did you get that?

30:53.351 --> 30:55.520
What do you mean, where?
It's my emergency snack.

30:55.604 --> 30:57.522
-Do you carry around jerky?
-Yes.

30:57.606 --> 30:59.983
I've got crispy rice snacks, gummies,
and some red ginseng.

31:00.067 --> 31:01.193
Tell me if you get hungry.

31:01.276 --> 31:03.445
[chuckling] You're like
a walking convenience store.

31:04.362 --> 31:06.281
It looks heavy.
Do you want me to carry it for you?

31:06.698 --> 31:08.617
-I'm fine.
-Come on. Let me.

31:09.785 --> 31:11.369
It's really okay. [chuckles softly]

31:12.412 --> 31:13.413
It's heavy.

31:13.497 --> 31:16.249
Those shoulders look sturdy.
You should carry it.

31:17.501 --> 31:18.585
[chuckles softly]

31:20.462 --> 31:21.797
Here.

31:21.880 --> 31:24.049
[grunts] This is for the jerky.

31:28.095 --> 31:30.514
We also just wrapped up. Heading home now.

31:31.014 --> 31:34.684
Mr. Han and Sejung are
also clocking out right at the site.

31:35.977 --> 31:37.687
Okay, I'll see you tomorrow.

31:38.605 --> 31:39.606
[line disconnects]

31:39.689 --> 31:41.691
Ms. Oh and Songhee said
they've completed the retrieval.

31:41.775 --> 31:42.818
[hums thoughtfully]

31:43.068 --> 31:44.069
Are you heading home?

31:44.653 --> 31:47.614
Actually, I need to go back to the office.

31:48.156 --> 31:49.658
I have a draft to send over.

31:49.741 --> 31:50.992
[exclaims thoughtfully]

31:51.076 --> 31:52.619
I'll drop you off.

31:53.703 --> 31:54.830
[phone vibrating]

31:55.413 --> 31:57.082
WOOJU

31:58.917 --> 32:00.335
[phone continues vibrating]

32:01.253 --> 32:02.504
It's Kim Wooju.

32:03.255 --> 32:04.297
Pick it up.

32:04.756 --> 32:06.341
We should find out why he's calling.

32:06.424 --> 32:08.093
I met with him already.

32:08.718 --> 32:10.345
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

32:11.346 --> 32:12.597
[phone continues vibrating]

32:18.145 --> 32:19.521
-[line ringing]
-[sighs worriedly]

32:23.024 --> 32:25.235
[sighs] Please pick up.

32:27.237 --> 32:28.363
[continues ringing]

32:28.446 --> 32:31.366
[automated voice] The call can't
be connected. Transferring to voicemail.

32:31.449 --> 32:32.951
-[line disconnects]
-[sighs wearily]

32:33.201 --> 32:35.078
She's not picking up her phone again.

32:37.539 --> 32:38.832
[♪ ominous music playing]

32:39.749 --> 32:42.002
Oh, my gosh. You startled me.

32:43.753 --> 32:44.880
What do you want with Meri?

32:46.214 --> 32:47.883
Don't listen in on other people's calls.

32:49.509 --> 32:50.510
Are you going somewhere?

32:50.594 --> 32:52.888
I'm flying to Japan with Mom tonight.

32:52.971 --> 32:53.972
To Beppu Onsen.

32:54.055 --> 32:55.432
[sighs] When are you coming back?

32:55.515 --> 32:58.059
It's a three-day package trip. [snickers]

32:58.560 --> 33:01.188
-There's beef bone soup in the fridge.
-Okay.

33:03.773 --> 33:07.277
Don't even think
about contacting Meri again.

33:08.111 --> 33:10.363
If she finds out
that you're marrying a rich girl,

33:10.447 --> 33:12.407
she might cause a scene at the wedding.

33:13.283 --> 33:17.787
She's probably already fuming
because Mom and her mom had a fight.

33:18.079 --> 33:19.873
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

33:20.874 --> 33:22.500
Mom met with Meri's mom?

33:22.584 --> 33:24.211
-When?
-What do you mean, when?

33:24.294 --> 33:25.629
When you were in Hong Kong.

33:25.712 --> 33:29.257
It seemed like Meri hadn't told her mom
that you guys broke off the engagement.

33:29.341 --> 33:32.093
So, Mom went berserk there and then.

33:32.177 --> 33:34.179
Why would you do that?

33:34.262 --> 33:36.681
What do you mean?
It was to stop her from clinging to you.

33:36.765 --> 33:38.600
Geez, I can't believe this!

33:39.059 --> 33:40.477
No wonder.

33:40.560 --> 33:42.270
That's why Meri is so mad.

33:42.646 --> 33:44.856
If she doesn't forgive me,
it's all your and Mom's fault.

33:44.940 --> 33:46.691
Go and be ready to apologize, okay?

33:48.235 --> 33:49.819
Where are you going?

33:49.903 --> 33:52.239
Aren't you going to drop us off
at the airport?

33:54.157 --> 33:55.158
Hi, Songhee.

33:55.242 --> 33:58.328
I can't get a hold of Meri.
Do you know where she is right now?

34:01.706 --> 34:03.291
Oh, we had a small argument.

34:04.834 --> 34:05.835
You know.

34:05.919 --> 34:07.254
Just a lovers' quarrel.

34:07.337 --> 34:08.463
[exclaims in realization]

34:08.546 --> 34:11.967
She's out on business right now,
so she might be hard to reach.

34:13.009 --> 34:15.220
There's been an incident at Myungsoondang.

34:16.096 --> 34:17.639
It's one of our clients.

34:17.722 --> 34:20.725
She's probably
with the team leader from there.

34:20.934 --> 34:21.935
The office?

34:22.018 --> 34:24.229
Yes, I think she'll head to the office
once she's done.

34:24.729 --> 34:25.730
I see. Thank you.

34:25.814 --> 34:27.357
I'll treat you to a meal later.

34:28.483 --> 34:29.484
[line disconnects]

34:32.779 --> 34:33.822
[seat belt clicks]

34:38.034 --> 34:40.537
PLEASE FIND THE ATTACHED
DESIGN DRAFT YOU REQUESTED

34:40.620 --> 34:42.914
DESIGN DRAFT B
DESIGN DRAFT A

34:45.292 --> 34:46.418
[Kim Wooju] That's a relief.

34:46.876 --> 34:48.753
That Wooju doesn't know anything.

34:49.421 --> 34:51.464
But you know there's still a risk, right?

34:52.173 --> 34:53.174
Of course.

34:54.050 --> 34:55.051
By the way,

34:55.468 --> 34:57.679
did you mean what you said back then?

34:58.013 --> 34:59.014
About what?

34:59.764 --> 35:03.143
That you wouldn't team up with Wooju
even if you had to get caught.

35:03.852 --> 35:05.520
Oh, that.

35:06.730 --> 35:08.106
I just said it in the moment.

35:08.815 --> 35:10.400
[acknowledges] Right?

35:10.692 --> 35:12.402
I did say it in the heat of the moment,

35:13.403 --> 35:14.404
but I'm sticking with it.

35:15.280 --> 35:16.323
You see,

35:16.781 --> 35:19.326
I thought it through after what you said.

35:19.409 --> 35:21.620
[sighs] It's a lot of money.

35:21.953 --> 35:23.371
What wouldn't I do for it?

35:24.831 --> 35:25.832
But I just couldn't.

35:30.587 --> 35:32.505
I know. I seem pathetic, don't I?

35:33.381 --> 35:35.091
That's just me.

35:35.175 --> 35:37.844
I'm the kind
who just goes all in, no brakes.

35:39.554 --> 35:40.597
[inhales deeply]

35:40.680 --> 35:41.681
We'll do it together.

35:43.016 --> 35:46.311
Come to think of it,
Wooju hasn't done anything.

35:46.394 --> 35:48.521
You entered the raffle.

35:48.605 --> 35:49.939
And you won the raffle.

35:50.023 --> 35:51.608
I went to the ceremony with you.

35:52.233 --> 35:54.944
It feels wrong for someone
who did nothing to profit from it.

35:55.028 --> 35:56.571
We did all the work.

35:59.240 --> 36:00.325
Mr. Kim.

36:00.408 --> 36:02.369
Thank you so much.

36:02.911 --> 36:05.830
I won't ever forget
what you've done for me.

36:05.914 --> 36:07.624
[♪ dreamy, orchestral music playing]

36:08.083 --> 36:11.086
I was actually really nervous
this whole time.

36:11.544 --> 36:14.255
In case you'd say you want out.

36:16.883 --> 36:19.803
I was really struggling,
but I couldn't tell anyone.

36:28.353 --> 36:29.437
[gasps]

36:30.772 --> 36:35.193
I'm really going to do my best,
so you hang in there, too.

36:35.276 --> 36:36.569
We're close to the end.

36:37.278 --> 36:38.822
[claps hands] Okay.

36:38.905 --> 36:40.865
Then I'll trust you and go with it, okay?

36:41.658 --> 36:42.659
Okay.

36:45.412 --> 36:46.830
[both chuckle]

36:51.334 --> 36:52.919
[sensor beeping]

36:59.467 --> 37:01.511
-[Kim Wooju] On the left.
-[Meri] I see it.

37:02.721 --> 37:03.722
[car alarm chirps]

37:06.683 --> 37:07.684
Who's that?

37:10.937 --> 37:12.063
[engine starts]

37:15.150 --> 37:16.484
[tires screech]

37:17.694 --> 37:19.529
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

38:07.744 --> 38:08.995
Where are they going?

38:18.338 --> 38:20.507
NO UNAUTHORIZED ENTRY

38:41.110 --> 38:42.278
[knocking at window]

38:45.323 --> 38:46.366
Are you a resident?

38:47.492 --> 38:50.495
[hesitates] I'm not. I'm just visiting.

38:50.578 --> 38:51.871
Visiting which house?

38:53.039 --> 38:54.040
Well...

38:54.332 --> 38:55.875
[Jenny] This is my aunt's address.

38:55.959 --> 38:57.502
Unit 2 of Complex 3 at Beauté Palace.

38:58.795 --> 39:00.004
Unit 2 of Complex 3.

39:00.088 --> 39:01.214
Okay.

39:09.764 --> 39:10.890
[Meri clears throat]

39:16.604 --> 39:18.273
Thank you for dropping me off.

39:18.356 --> 39:19.899
-Drive home safe.
-Okay.

39:19.983 --> 39:21.442
I'll leave after I see you head in.

39:21.526 --> 39:23.194
No, you should get going.

39:23.278 --> 39:24.904
I'll get going after I see you go in.

39:24.988 --> 39:27.240
I'll go in after I see you get going.

39:27.866 --> 39:28.992
All right, then.

39:29.075 --> 39:30.827
-[Sanghyeon] Yes.
-[door closes]

39:30.910 --> 39:33.830
Yes, I'm on my way now.
I'll look for it in the car.

39:34.372 --> 39:35.373
Okay.

39:35.456 --> 39:36.791
[♪ tense, whimsical music playing]

39:42.046 --> 39:43.381
-[gate clatters]
-[grunts softly]

39:48.386 --> 39:49.387
[gate clangs]

40:02.442 --> 40:05.778
Gosh, he's standing right there,
so I can't get going.

40:06.279 --> 40:08.197
[Meri sighs deeply]

40:08.698 --> 40:10.575
You should leave a bit later.

40:10.658 --> 40:13.244
Since there was a mistake
in the deliveries today,

40:13.328 --> 40:15.955
someone might need to ask something.

40:16.039 --> 40:17.040
Shall I?

40:17.540 --> 40:18.875
I'll leave later, then.

40:19.417 --> 40:20.543
[sharp inhale]

40:21.336 --> 40:22.337
[exhales]

40:22.420 --> 40:25.298
Do you need any hammering or fixing done?

40:26.049 --> 40:27.175
No, I'm okay.

40:27.258 --> 40:29.260
The management office
sorts it out for me if I ask.

40:29.344 --> 40:32.138
Gosh, what if they catch you living alone?

40:32.221 --> 40:33.348
Tell me while I'm here.

40:33.640 --> 40:35.850
[chuckles] There isn't anything.

40:39.312 --> 40:40.313
What's that?

40:44.150 --> 40:45.443
[hesitates]

40:46.361 --> 40:49.405
I can hang the curtains myself
since you installed the bar for me.

40:49.489 --> 40:50.907
It's fine.

40:51.699 --> 40:53.660
This is when a husband comes in handy.

40:54.494 --> 40:55.995
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

40:58.581 --> 40:59.624
"Husband"?

41:00.458 --> 41:04.337
Oh, no. That's not what I meant.

41:04.420 --> 41:05.713
[stutters] I mean...

41:07.340 --> 41:08.633
[gasps, screams]

41:08.716 --> 41:10.134
[♪ comical music playing]

41:18.893 --> 41:20.353
Oh, gosh. Are you okay?

41:21.688 --> 41:23.147
Are you okay?

41:23.940 --> 41:25.400
Yes, I'm fine.

41:26.275 --> 41:28.236
-Are you really okay?
-Yes.

41:32.448 --> 41:35.159
Oh, no. Your clothes are all wet.

41:35.702 --> 41:37.578
I'll do it. Don't worry about it.

41:38.371 --> 41:40.039
[♪ enthralling orchestral music playing]

41:40.123 --> 41:41.207
[hesitates]

41:42.709 --> 41:43.751
It's okay.

41:43.835 --> 41:46.629
I'll dry this while you dry your hair.

41:46.713 --> 41:47.714
Okay, then.

41:50.758 --> 41:52.051
I'm sure it'll dry soon.

41:53.970 --> 41:56.931
By the way, just call me
if you ever need someone tall.

41:57.015 --> 41:58.016
[chuckles] Okay.

42:01.436 --> 42:02.729
What are you doing tomorrow?

42:02.812 --> 42:05.064
I don't have anything tomorrow.

42:05.148 --> 42:06.274
[acknowledges]

42:07.442 --> 42:09.193
-Do you want...
-How about a lunch...

42:09.944 --> 42:10.987
[Kim Wooju chuckles softly]

42:13.072 --> 42:14.198
Let's get lunch tomorrow.

42:15.241 --> 42:16.242
Sure.

42:18.453 --> 42:19.495
[clears throat]

42:24.792 --> 42:26.085
[Wooju] Where did they go?

42:28.046 --> 42:30.214
I'm sure they went this way.

42:33.092 --> 42:34.302
That's 7794.

42:49.484 --> 42:51.861
[♪ dramatic sting]

42:53.988 --> 42:55.615
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

42:59.202 --> 43:00.369
That guy...

43:06.876 --> 43:08.002
[scoffs]

43:08.503 --> 43:09.837
What?

43:09.921 --> 43:11.672
So, it was Meri back then.

43:31.984 --> 43:33.361
What's with my expression?

43:33.778 --> 43:35.071
I look so tense.

43:36.030 --> 43:37.115
[sharp inhale]

43:37.573 --> 43:40.576
Next time we retake it,
I'll try to be more natural...

43:41.661 --> 43:42.662
[chuckles softly]

43:42.954 --> 43:44.789
Why would we retake it?

43:45.498 --> 43:47.708
[inhales deeply, exhales]

43:47.792 --> 43:49.502
[♪ enchanting music playing]

43:57.677 --> 43:59.512
He's out of my league.

44:28.791 --> 44:30.251
[Wooju] Yoo Meri.

44:35.214 --> 44:36.757
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

44:37.758 --> 44:38.759
Kim Wooju.

44:49.854 --> 44:50.897
What are you doing here?

44:51.480 --> 44:52.899
And who was that man before?

44:52.982 --> 44:54.108
The one who dropped you off.

44:57.403 --> 44:58.738
Did you follow me?

45:00.072 --> 45:01.490
Yes.

45:01.574 --> 45:03.993
I went to your office
because you wouldn't pick up my calls.

45:04.076 --> 45:06.245
But then you got in some guy's car.

45:08.664 --> 45:10.416
And you two went into this house.

45:16.756 --> 45:19.592
That day, you saw me, didn't you?

45:19.675 --> 45:21.052
On the roof.

45:24.639 --> 45:25.723
[scoffs]

45:26.140 --> 45:27.141
You did.

45:28.226 --> 45:29.560
Why did you lie?

45:29.644 --> 45:30.645
You said you worked.

45:30.728 --> 45:33.564
I didn't want to tell you where I lived.

45:33.648 --> 45:34.690
You live here?

45:36.317 --> 45:39.111
You lost everything in that rental con,
so how are you...

45:40.905 --> 45:42.031
No way. Are you...

45:42.114 --> 45:43.783
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

45:47.286 --> 45:48.746
working part-time?

45:48.829 --> 45:50.164
You work as a housekeeper?

45:51.832 --> 45:53.668
Yes, it's my friend's house.

45:54.543 --> 45:55.836
But because no one lives here,

45:55.920 --> 45:58.172
I'm currently managing it
while staying here.

45:58.798 --> 46:00.716
A friend? Who?

46:01.175 --> 46:02.385
None of your business.

46:09.642 --> 46:10.643
Is this that guy's house?

46:11.269 --> 46:12.270
It's not.

46:13.688 --> 46:14.689
[sighs]

46:15.564 --> 46:16.691
[exclaims anxiously]

46:17.692 --> 46:18.693
Leave.

46:19.944 --> 46:20.987
Open this.

46:25.616 --> 46:27.034
Then who was that guy?

46:27.118 --> 46:29.245
Why did he drop you off
this late at night?

46:29.328 --> 46:30.329
[Meri sighs]

46:30.413 --> 46:31.622
Are you cheating on me?

46:32.123 --> 46:33.207
[♪ melancholy music playing]

46:33.291 --> 46:35.584
[sighs] What you did is called cheating.

46:35.751 --> 46:38.504
Who I meet is none of your business.

46:41.340 --> 46:44.260
Meri, now I know why you're so angry.

46:47.638 --> 46:49.265
It's because of my mom.

46:49.348 --> 46:52.768
I'll apologize
for how my mom talked to yours.

46:52.852 --> 46:54.228
You don't need to.

46:54.312 --> 46:56.647
And I have nothing to do
with your family now.

46:58.024 --> 46:59.150
[gasps]

46:59.233 --> 47:01.152
I told you I'm sorry.

47:01.235 --> 47:03.154
How many times do I have to say it?

47:03.237 --> 47:04.697
Just accept the damn apology.

47:05.531 --> 47:06.574
What?

47:06.657 --> 47:07.992
Do you want me to kneel?

47:08.909 --> 47:10.036
Stop it.

47:10.119 --> 47:12.121
Why do I have to accept your apology?

47:12.204 --> 47:14.123
I don't want to, so stop apologizing.

47:14.832 --> 47:16.917
I don't need you or your apology anymore.

47:22.590 --> 47:24.008
[door keypad beeping]

47:25.676 --> 47:27.136
[♪ foreboding music playing]

47:27.636 --> 47:29.430
-[Meri screams]
-Move.

47:29.513 --> 47:31.724
Let go. What are you doing?

47:31.807 --> 47:33.434
You're acting like this
because you're guilty!

47:33.517 --> 47:34.769
-[screaming]
-[grunts]

47:38.981 --> 47:41.108
Get out. I'm going to call the police!

47:41.192 --> 47:42.902
Go on because I'm about to lose it.

47:44.028 --> 47:45.905
Are you crazy? What are you doing?

47:45.988 --> 47:47.531
Yes, I'm crazy.

47:47.615 --> 47:50.493
How could you start dating another man
only months after the breakup?

47:50.576 --> 47:51.994
Were you always like this?

47:52.078 --> 47:55.081
The house is that punk's, isn't it?

47:55.164 --> 47:57.792
He's also the one
you were with on the rooftop.

48:01.420 --> 48:02.463
[gasps softly]

48:02.838 --> 48:03.964
Look at you.

48:04.048 --> 48:05.091
You're flustered.

48:05.883 --> 48:07.301
I got you, didn't I?

48:08.344 --> 48:09.512
Got what?

48:09.595 --> 48:11.138
Get out now.

48:12.473 --> 48:15.810
Were you cheating on me with him?

48:16.769 --> 48:20.439
And yet you treated me
like a cheating scumbag?

48:21.315 --> 48:24.777
Let's see how well off
your rich boyfriend is.

48:24.860 --> 48:26.362
[♪ gripping, tense music playing]

48:49.468 --> 48:50.553
What's this?

48:52.388 --> 48:54.473
-Get out.
-What are you doing?

48:54.557 --> 48:56.725
-Get out!
-Let me go!

48:56.809 --> 48:58.144
I said, let go.

48:58.227 --> 48:59.395
Let me go!

48:59.478 --> 49:01.105
Let go!

49:01.188 --> 49:02.314
[grunts]

49:03.858 --> 49:05.025
[bone cracks]

49:05.276 --> 49:06.485
[groans]

49:06.569 --> 49:07.987
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

49:08.070 --> 49:09.488
[exclaiming in pain]

49:13.742 --> 49:15.202
[Wooju screaming in pain]

49:24.211 --> 49:25.629
[groaning]

49:25.713 --> 49:27.131
Doctor!

49:27.214 --> 49:29.175
[exclaiming in pain]

49:29.675 --> 49:31.677
I checked your CT scan.

49:31.760 --> 49:35.264
It seems you fractured your wrist
when you tried to break the fall.

49:35.973 --> 49:36.974
Fractured?

49:38.309 --> 49:39.894
There's just a small crack

49:39.977 --> 49:41.979
in your right pelvis and thigh,
not fractured.

49:42.480 --> 49:45.316
Let's admit you and keep an eye on it.

49:45.399 --> 49:46.400
A crack?

49:47.735 --> 49:48.736
Doctor, tell me...

49:49.487 --> 49:51.780
Am I going to be paralyzed
from the waist down?

49:51.864 --> 49:54.283
-[chuckles] It's not that bad.
-[groaning]

49:54.366 --> 49:57.661
For now, the guardian should assist
the patient when moving.

49:57.745 --> 50:00.247
A fall could turn that crack
into a full fracture.

50:00.998 --> 50:03.000
Okay, but I'm not his guardian.

50:03.083 --> 50:04.668
Meri!

50:04.919 --> 50:06.337
[exclaiming in pain]

50:06.420 --> 50:08.964
My arm hurts. Come here, hurry.

50:10.257 --> 50:11.258
What do you want?

50:11.342 --> 50:12.927
It hurts so much.

50:13.010 --> 50:14.303
What do you want me to do about it?

50:14.386 --> 50:15.638
Kiss it better.

50:20.851 --> 50:22.228
It seems the VVIPs' response

50:22.311 --> 50:24.772
to the founding anniversary gift
was quite good.

50:25.147 --> 50:27.107
Beauté contacted us
to express their gratitude.

50:27.191 --> 50:28.943
There was some trouble with the cards.

50:29.902 --> 50:30.903
That's right.

50:31.529 --> 50:33.405
I heard from Ms. Kim.

50:33.489 --> 50:35.074
I heard that Wooju handled it well.

50:36.075 --> 50:39.286
It's really thanks
to all the members of the marketing team.

50:39.828 --> 50:41.539
Do your best to support him.

50:42.081 --> 50:44.792
Your job is to help Wooju
lead Myungsoondang.

50:45.793 --> 50:47.753
That's why you're in that position.

50:47.836 --> 50:49.713
CEO KO PHILNYUN

50:52.550 --> 50:53.968
Of course, well noted.

50:59.139 --> 51:01.308
[♪ ominous music playing]

51:12.027 --> 51:13.320
[♪ ominous sting]

51:16.865 --> 51:17.866
Hello, sir.

51:19.368 --> 51:21.495
She's the wife of the late Mr. Ko.

51:23.497 --> 51:25.040
[crying, sniffles]

51:25.124 --> 51:28.127
[Hangu] I don't know
what to say to console you.

51:28.210 --> 51:29.587
[breath trembling]

51:29.670 --> 51:31.297
-Please stay strong.
-[sniffles]

51:32.006 --> 51:33.382
[gasps]

51:33.465 --> 51:35.050
Have you been well?

51:35.843 --> 51:36.844
Yes.

51:36.927 --> 51:38.637
[chuckles] What brings you here?

51:38.721 --> 51:39.847
To meet with the chairwoman.

51:40.639 --> 51:42.433
Let's go. She must be waiting.

51:42.516 --> 51:44.268
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

51:58.073 --> 51:59.408
[♪ dramatic sting]

52:02.328 --> 52:05.164
I found this while I was sorting out
my late husband's things.

52:05.247 --> 52:07.291
This was deep inside the drawer.

52:08.792 --> 52:10.919
It seemed important.

52:26.810 --> 52:27.936
[♪ tense music playing]

52:28.020 --> 52:30.648
FINANCIAL STATEMENT

52:42.868 --> 52:44.328
[♪ dramatic sting]

52:45.663 --> 52:47.206
210,000 TRANSFERRED

52:47.289 --> 52:48.791
[♪ tense music continues]

52:52.211 --> 52:53.462
CONSULTANT FEE
220,000 TRANSFERRED

52:53.545 --> 52:56.799
[Mr. Ko] It looks like J Consulting
is embezzling some of it.

52:57.341 --> 53:00.094
I found it odd
and contacted our US counterpart,

53:00.177 --> 53:03.722
and the company itself seems to have
exaggerated their performance.

53:04.390 --> 53:05.849
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

53:10.771 --> 53:11.855
[sighs wearily]

53:16.985 --> 53:18.696
J CONSULTING

53:19.530 --> 53:20.572
[line ringing]

53:21.156 --> 53:22.950
[♪ ominous sting]

53:27.329 --> 53:29.039
CONSULTANT FEE

53:29.123 --> 53:30.416
[phone ringing]

53:34.169 --> 53:35.212
Yes, dear.

53:35.963 --> 53:37.423
What made you call me at this hour?

53:38.549 --> 53:40.342
I was just balancing the books.

53:40.801 --> 53:43.429
I have to send it to Myungsoondang
by the end of this week.

53:46.515 --> 53:48.183
What do you mean, clean up the accounts?

53:48.267 --> 53:51.729
Mr. Ko's wife came to the company
to meet with the chairwoman.

53:51.812 --> 53:55.107
Start by shredding every company document,
and proceed with the business closure.

53:55.190 --> 53:56.734
Also, close down the restaurant.

53:57.776 --> 53:58.819
Okay.

53:58.902 --> 54:00.612
No harm in being cautious.

54:00.696 --> 54:01.864
[♪ tense music playing]

54:01.947 --> 54:04.950
But the chairwoman
doesn't know about this, right?

54:07.202 --> 54:08.954
[mumbles]

54:10.372 --> 54:11.707
Mom.

54:12.916 --> 54:14.460
Sweetie, you're up.

54:17.504 --> 54:19.006
Do you want to talk to Dad?

54:19.089 --> 54:20.174
Daddy?

54:21.383 --> 54:22.593
Daddy.

54:23.010 --> 54:25.804
Henry, did you just wake up?

54:25.888 --> 54:27.139
How's your cold?

54:27.473 --> 54:31.185
[gasps] You're all better now?
What a good boy.

54:31.268 --> 54:32.978
Daddy will go back to the US soon.

54:33.061 --> 54:35.439
Stay healthy so we can go camping again.
[chuckles]

54:35.773 --> 54:37.524
Be good and listen to your mom.

54:37.608 --> 54:39.860
[in English] I can't wait
to see you, Daddy.

54:40.277 --> 54:41.862
[chuckles] Me too.

54:42.654 --> 54:44.198
[♪ ominous music playing]

54:46.533 --> 54:47.576
[line disconnects]

54:49.745 --> 54:51.246
[♪ music increases in tempo]

54:54.458 --> 54:55.667
[knocking at door]

54:57.294 --> 54:58.420
Director Jang, are you busy?

54:58.504 --> 54:59.838
No, come in.

54:59.922 --> 55:01.381
CFO JANG HANGU

55:03.300 --> 55:04.676
I was just waiting for you.

55:07.387 --> 55:09.139
[in English] Thank you.

55:09.848 --> 55:12.059
[in Korean] You can drop the formality
when it's just us.

55:12.518 --> 55:14.728
Oh, okay. Uncle. [chuckles]

55:14.811 --> 55:17.481
Good work on sorting the issue out
for Beauté Department Store.

55:17.564 --> 55:20.567
I've cleared things up with them,
so don't worry.

55:20.651 --> 55:23.946
They could've made this into a big deal.

55:24.029 --> 55:26.782
But it seems to have gone over smoothly,
all thanks to you.

55:26.865 --> 55:28.742
Come to me
if you ever face any trouble again.

55:28.825 --> 55:30.160
I can help you.

55:30.994 --> 55:32.579
Okay. [chuckles softly]

55:34.081 --> 55:35.123
This isn't ours.

55:35.999 --> 55:38.001
I got it from a café across the street.

55:38.085 --> 55:39.461
It's tastier than ours.

55:39.545 --> 55:40.629
Drink this in secret.

55:40.712 --> 55:41.713
[chuckles]

55:42.714 --> 55:43.715
Thanks.

55:43.799 --> 55:44.925
[both chuckle]

55:47.886 --> 55:48.971
[gasps]

55:50.514 --> 55:51.682
[chuckles nervously]

55:52.140 --> 55:53.141
[exclaims in frustration]

55:53.225 --> 55:54.226
[in English] Thank you. Thank you.

55:55.227 --> 55:56.853
[in Korean] Gosh, my documents...

55:59.398 --> 56:00.941
J Consulting America COMPANY FINANCIALS

56:01.024 --> 56:02.150
[♪ tense music playing]

56:03.193 --> 56:04.444
-It's fine now.
-Oh, okay.

56:06.863 --> 56:08.740
-I'll get going then.
-Okay, thanks.

56:13.996 --> 56:15.372
[breathing heavily]

56:17.374 --> 56:18.458
[exclaims]

56:18.542 --> 56:20.419
[Wooju] Oh, be gentle. [groans]

56:20.752 --> 56:21.753
Seriously.

56:22.879 --> 56:24.298
Meri, my leg.

56:24.381 --> 56:25.507
[exclaiming in pain]

56:25.591 --> 56:27.551
[groans] Be gentle!

56:29.970 --> 56:31.013
[groans]

56:31.555 --> 56:33.348
[panting]

56:35.309 --> 56:36.977
[groans] Thank you.

56:38.645 --> 56:40.063
You still can't reach your mom?

56:40.147 --> 56:43.066
No, I don't think she enabled roaming.

56:43.150 --> 56:44.776
And my sister's phone is turned off.

56:44.860 --> 56:46.028
What about your dad?

56:46.111 --> 56:49.364
You know he got dismissed
from the university and started farming.

56:50.449 --> 56:53.619
He's been lying low alone in Jeju,
but he's also not very well.

56:56.038 --> 56:58.874
Hey, shouldn't you stay with me for a bit?

56:59.499 --> 57:02.419
Technically, I slipped
because you turned off the lights.

57:03.253 --> 57:04.254
[scoffs]

57:04.630 --> 57:05.881
Are you serious?

57:06.256 --> 57:08.342
You're the one who trespassed.

57:08.842 --> 57:10.093
That's a crime.

57:10.177 --> 57:11.595
I could report you to the police.

57:11.678 --> 57:13.722
Since when did you become so heartless?

57:13.805 --> 57:14.931
You weren't like this before.

57:15.015 --> 57:16.141
Yes, I was.

57:16.558 --> 57:18.352
I've always been heartless
to people I don't like.

57:21.730 --> 57:23.649
-[exclaiming in pain] Meri.
-What?

57:23.732 --> 57:25.150
Meri, here. [groans]

57:26.068 --> 57:27.235
[stomach rumbles]

57:28.779 --> 57:31.031
Being in pain is making me hungrier.

57:33.033 --> 57:35.577
I saw a sundae soup place downstairs.

57:35.661 --> 57:37.621
Could you pick some up for me?

57:37.704 --> 57:39.998
You've got a lot of nerve, seriously.

57:40.832 --> 57:42.584
[Jingyeong] I had it cleaned.

57:43.168 --> 57:44.795
Thank you for that day.

57:45.170 --> 57:46.588
From Yoon Jingyeong.

57:54.388 --> 57:56.306
[sighs] Where did he go?

57:56.640 --> 57:58.308
I need to give this back to him.

58:01.395 --> 58:02.479
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

58:02.562 --> 58:03.605
[groaning]

58:07.067 --> 58:08.860
Illegal filming carries
up to seven years in prison

58:08.944 --> 58:10.195
and a 50-million-won fine.

58:11.071 --> 58:12.948
If forensics reveals more,

58:14.074 --> 58:16.076
you'll be charged
as a repeat offender with no leniency.

58:17.119 --> 58:19.746
I'll let you off
since it looks like your first time.

58:20.914 --> 58:22.249
But I won't the next time.

58:25.210 --> 58:27.129
What is he, really?

58:29.881 --> 58:31.425
He's such a mystery.

58:32.884 --> 58:36.555
YOON JINGYEONG
DOCTOR OF FAMILY MEDICINE

58:36.638 --> 58:38.640
REAL FRUIT JUICE
GUMMIES

58:49.192 --> 58:51.528
I've been saving this, but it's my treat

58:52.487 --> 58:53.947
since I am grateful.

58:58.827 --> 58:59.911
[elevator dings]

59:09.713 --> 59:10.797
[elevator dings]

59:21.183 --> 59:22.267
[Wooju exclaims]

59:27.773 --> 59:28.774
[sighs]

59:39.034 --> 59:40.118
[chuckles softly]

59:44.539 --> 59:45.874
Do you know?

59:45.957 --> 59:47.918
You're the first person
to introduce me to sundae soup.

59:48.835 --> 59:52.088
You took me to that famous place
in the Jongno underground.

59:52.672 --> 59:54.216
I couldn't even eat such things back...

59:55.091 --> 59:56.092
It's hot.

59:59.930 --> 01:00:00.931
[chuckles softly]

01:00:02.474 --> 01:00:03.683
Looking back,

01:00:03.767 --> 01:00:05.477
I discovered a lot of things
thanks to you.

01:00:06.770 --> 01:00:10.148
You also showed me that you can eat
steamed sweet potatoes with their peel.

01:00:10.232 --> 01:00:12.067
I was taught to peel everything.

01:00:12.859 --> 01:00:14.110
[sighs]

01:00:14.194 --> 01:00:16.696
It looks like I taught you
so many useful things.

01:00:17.989 --> 01:00:19.533
So, I'm always grateful to you.

01:00:20.534 --> 01:00:22.828
You always teach me new things.

01:00:25.705 --> 01:00:29.334
Being in the hospital reminds me of this.

01:00:30.043 --> 01:00:33.547
In the human body,
they say there are 30 trillion cells.

01:00:34.381 --> 01:00:36.007
And 330 billion of them

01:00:36.633 --> 01:00:39.219
die and regenerate daily.

01:00:39.511 --> 01:00:40.762
[♪ whimsical music playing]

01:00:40.846 --> 01:00:44.474
The cells that let you down
a few months ago don't exist anymore.

01:00:44.558 --> 01:00:45.642
They're all gone.

01:00:45.725 --> 01:00:48.395
Now I'm completely made up of new cells.

01:00:48.478 --> 01:00:49.896
I'm a new person.

01:00:51.857 --> 01:00:54.442
So, Meri, let's forget the past

01:00:55.318 --> 01:00:56.570
and start anew.

01:00:59.322 --> 01:01:00.448
[in English] Okay.

01:01:00.532 --> 01:01:03.326
[in Korean] I'll be cool and forgive you
for that brief fling with another guy.

01:01:03.410 --> 01:01:04.786
It's not like I'm all that innocent.

01:01:05.328 --> 01:01:06.413
So, let's be generous

01:01:07.455 --> 01:01:08.707
and just call it even.

01:01:13.962 --> 01:01:15.547
What are you trying to pull?

01:01:15.630 --> 01:01:17.048
People don't change.

01:01:18.884 --> 01:01:20.510
Are you done? I'm cleaning up now.

01:01:20.594 --> 01:01:23.096
I'm not done. Hey.

01:01:23.179 --> 01:01:24.180
[exclaims]

01:01:24.264 --> 01:01:25.932
I thought you were done
since you kept talking.

01:01:26.016 --> 01:01:27.183
No, I'm sorry.

01:01:27.267 --> 01:01:29.561
Just another bite, please.

01:01:29.644 --> 01:01:30.937
Please?

01:01:33.231 --> 01:01:34.691
Eat it yourself then.

01:01:35.650 --> 01:01:36.818
Hey, Meri.

01:01:36.902 --> 01:01:38.320
Hey, Meri!

01:01:39.446 --> 01:01:41.156
[door opens, closes]

01:01:43.074 --> 01:01:45.035
Was the cell metaphor lame?

01:01:45.118 --> 01:01:46.494
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

01:01:48.788 --> 01:01:49.873
[sighs softly]

01:01:49.956 --> 01:01:51.416
[Kim Wooju] What are you doing tomorrow?

01:01:51.583 --> 01:01:53.335
-Do you want...
-How about a lunch...

01:01:56.046 --> 01:01:57.213
Let's get lunch tomorrow.

01:01:58.048 --> 01:01:59.090
Sure.

01:02:00.592 --> 01:02:01.635
[clears throat]

01:02:09.809 --> 01:02:12.312
-I'll order when my company arrives.
-Sure.

01:02:32.624 --> 01:02:33.667
Hello.

01:02:34.376 --> 01:02:35.418
[acknowledges]

01:02:35.502 --> 01:02:37.545
I guess he hasn't been discharged yet.

01:02:37.879 --> 01:02:38.880
[hesitates]

01:02:38.964 --> 01:02:40.048
He will tomorrow.

01:02:40.131 --> 01:02:41.257
[hums thoughtfully]

01:02:45.679 --> 01:02:47.430
Your jacket. The windbreaker.

01:02:48.515 --> 01:02:49.641
[acknowledges]

01:02:56.940 --> 01:02:59.609
Oh, that's just my way
of saying thank you.

01:03:02.529 --> 01:03:05.198
You seemed pretty skilled at CPR.
Did you learn from somewhere?

01:03:06.408 --> 01:03:08.034
When I was still a student,

01:03:08.118 --> 01:03:10.954
I worked part-time as safety staff
at an amusement park.

01:03:11.037 --> 01:03:12.080
[hums thoughtfully]

01:03:12.831 --> 01:03:14.791
Anyway, thank you for that day.

01:03:14.874 --> 01:03:15.875
Personally, too.

01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:19.963
I saw you make them delete my photos.

01:03:20.630 --> 01:03:22.215
[♪ gentle whimsical music playing]

01:03:23.967 --> 01:03:25.176
Thank you.

01:03:26.344 --> 01:03:28.388
I can't grant an extension
to the hospital stay,

01:03:28.471 --> 01:03:31.099
but I'll keep a bottle of liquor for you
at your usual bar.

01:03:31.683 --> 01:03:33.309
Enjoy it when you have time.

01:03:33.393 --> 01:03:34.477
It's my token of gratitude.

01:03:34.561 --> 01:03:35.603
It's okay.

01:03:35.687 --> 01:03:37.272
It wasn't a big deal.

01:03:37.355 --> 01:03:38.857
Anyone would've done the same.

01:03:39.566 --> 01:03:40.567
So, no need.

01:03:41.651 --> 01:03:43.903
No, I... Wait.

01:03:48.199 --> 01:03:49.409
[sighs deeply]

01:03:50.744 --> 01:03:54.831
I haven't confessed to him,
but why does it feel like I got dumped?

01:03:57.459 --> 01:03:58.668
That felt oddly unsettling.

01:04:02.005 --> 01:04:04.215
[♪ soft jazz music playing in background]

01:04:14.309 --> 01:04:15.310
[sighs]

01:04:25.028 --> 01:04:26.237
[line ringing]

01:04:28.031 --> 01:04:29.074
Oh, right.

01:04:29.824 --> 01:04:30.867
I'm so sorry.

01:04:31.409 --> 01:04:32.494
I completely forgot.

01:04:32.577 --> 01:04:34.412
[acknowledges] Is that so?

01:04:35.455 --> 01:04:37.457
-Did you have lunch then?
-No.

01:04:37.540 --> 01:04:39.501
I'm currently at the hospital.

01:04:39.918 --> 01:04:41.878
[exclaims quizzically] Are you sick?

01:04:42.629 --> 01:04:44.255
No, not me. It's...

01:04:46.216 --> 01:04:48.593
[hesitates] My friend got hurt.

01:04:49.969 --> 01:04:53.473
I was busy nursing all through the night,
so I forgot to call you.

01:04:53.765 --> 01:04:54.933
[hums thoughtfully]

01:04:56.101 --> 01:04:58.186
Was your friend hurt badly?

01:04:59.312 --> 01:05:02.357
It's okay. We can eat together next time.

01:05:02.440 --> 01:05:04.943
Don't worry about me
and focus on nursing your friend.

01:05:05.026 --> 01:05:07.445
It's miserable
when there's no one around while sick.

01:05:09.280 --> 01:05:10.365
Okay.

01:05:10.448 --> 01:05:11.658
[♪ melancholy music playing]

01:05:11.741 --> 01:05:12.742
[line disconnects]

01:05:17.288 --> 01:05:18.289
[clicks tongue]

01:05:19.999 --> 01:05:21.000
[phone vibrating]

01:05:23.253 --> 01:05:24.504
JINGYEONG

01:05:25.004 --> 01:05:26.047
[chuckles softly]

01:05:26.756 --> 01:05:28.007
[line ringing, connects]

01:05:28.716 --> 01:05:30.218
Hey, Wooju. Did you eat?

01:05:30.301 --> 01:05:31.761
No, not yet.

01:05:31.845 --> 01:05:33.596
You haven't? What were you doing?

01:05:33.680 --> 01:05:35.098
-What about you?
-Me?

01:05:35.181 --> 01:05:36.683
I most certainly...

01:05:38.434 --> 01:05:39.936
have not eaten yet.

01:05:40.019 --> 01:05:41.146
Do you want to eat together?

01:05:41.229 --> 01:05:43.439
Sure, let's grab lunch together.

01:05:44.524 --> 01:05:45.525
I'll go to you.

01:05:45.608 --> 01:05:47.944
It'll be a break-time
by the time you get here.

01:05:48.778 --> 01:05:49.779
Okay.

01:05:51.823 --> 01:05:52.866
[line disconnects]

01:05:52.949 --> 01:05:53.992
[clicks tongue]

01:05:55.577 --> 01:05:56.578
Meri.

01:06:02.792 --> 01:06:03.877
[groans]

01:06:06.671 --> 01:06:07.964
Come closer, will you?

01:06:10.091 --> 01:06:11.217
[Meri sighs]

01:06:11.593 --> 01:06:12.719
[Wooju groans]

01:06:13.720 --> 01:06:17.807
I wouldn't even have been able to go
to the bathroom without you.

01:06:18.683 --> 01:06:20.435
Call in a caregiver tomorrow.

01:06:21.352 --> 01:06:22.896
They're uncomfortable.

01:06:23.855 --> 01:06:25.565
If I'm at unease--

01:06:25.648 --> 01:06:27.317
You're not dying.

01:06:27.734 --> 01:06:29.652
I'm busy. I don't have time for you.

01:06:30.403 --> 01:06:32.822
And if you keep this up,
I'm going to report you for trespassing.

01:06:32.906 --> 01:06:33.990
[exclaiming in pain]

01:06:34.490 --> 01:06:35.867
[groans, pants]

01:06:38.912 --> 01:06:40.038
[sighs]

01:06:40.246 --> 01:06:41.247
But I'm in pain.

01:06:42.999 --> 01:06:44.125
[sighs]

01:06:45.919 --> 01:06:47.253
[groaning]

01:06:57.263 --> 01:06:58.932
[♪ dreamy pop music playing]

01:07:00.266 --> 01:07:01.392
Mr. Kim.

01:07:07.023 --> 01:07:08.024
You...

01:07:19.994 --> 01:07:21.079
What are you doing?

01:07:23.331 --> 01:07:26.251
That's the friend who got hurt?

01:07:27.085 --> 01:07:28.086
Yes.

01:07:35.802 --> 01:07:36.886
[Wooju exclaims quizzically]

01:07:36.970 --> 01:07:39.138
What are you doing?
I'm a patient, so don't do anything.

01:07:39.222 --> 01:07:40.348
Where is his room?

01:07:40.932 --> 01:07:43.142
It's Room 601.

01:07:43.226 --> 01:07:45.853
I told you to call me
if you need someone tall.

01:07:48.439 --> 01:07:49.482
Let me go.

01:07:49.565 --> 01:07:51.150
I said, let go!

01:07:51.234 --> 01:07:52.735
Hey, Meri!

01:07:52.819 --> 01:07:54.279
[screaming]

01:07:54.362 --> 01:07:55.363
Meri!

01:07:55.446 --> 01:07:56.489
Let me go!

01:07:57.573 --> 01:07:58.866
Meri!

01:07:59.701 --> 01:08:01.744
Yoo Meri! Meri!

01:08:03.121 --> 01:08:04.539
[Wooju exclaiming in pain]

01:08:11.212 --> 01:08:15.300
I'm sorry for not telling you
that it was Kim Wooju.

01:08:15.758 --> 01:08:16.968
And for not showing up to lunch.

01:08:17.468 --> 01:08:19.137
Did you get any sleep?

01:08:19.220 --> 01:08:20.471
You said you were up all night.

01:08:20.555 --> 01:08:22.557
I'll get some sleep now.

01:08:22.640 --> 01:08:24.517
Then, go get some sleep.

01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:26.144
Let's talk more
when you're feeling better.

01:08:26.811 --> 01:08:28.354
Are you angry?

01:08:31.482 --> 01:08:32.692
I'm not angry.

01:08:33.609 --> 01:08:35.403
But I'm not feeling great, either.

01:08:38.865 --> 01:08:41.159
I mean, why didn't you call me yesterday?

01:08:42.243 --> 01:08:43.995
Or you could have told me earlier today.

01:08:45.038 --> 01:08:47.665
[chuckles softly]
I'm always asking you for a favor.

01:08:47.749 --> 01:08:50.209
How can I ask you to come for Kim Wooju?

01:08:50.293 --> 01:08:52.045
Do you have to nurse him?

01:08:53.004 --> 01:08:55.673
It's not like I wanted to do it, either.

01:08:55.757 --> 01:08:59.385
He's throwing a fit,
and we couldn't reach his family.

01:08:59.469 --> 01:09:01.012
So, I couldn't just leave him alone.

01:09:01.095 --> 01:09:02.430
Just leave him.

01:09:02.513 --> 01:09:04.724
Why do you care for such a person?

01:09:04.807 --> 01:09:08.019
After all you went through,
do you still have feelings for him?

01:09:08.102 --> 01:09:09.103
No.

01:09:09.562 --> 01:09:10.563
It's because...

01:09:11.564 --> 01:09:12.565
[sighs]

01:09:13.149 --> 01:09:15.943
If I just left,
he'd lose it and cause trouble.

01:09:16.027 --> 01:09:18.696
It seemed like he'd do anything
to find that house's owner.

01:09:19.697 --> 01:09:20.740
Also...

01:09:21.866 --> 01:09:25.411
Even if it didn't end well with him,
he was hurt in front of me.

01:09:27.497 --> 01:09:28.748
Wait.

01:09:28.831 --> 01:09:30.416
Last time,

01:09:31.542 --> 01:09:33.795
didn't you say to team up with Wooju
if push came to shove?

01:09:34.420 --> 01:09:35.421
I did.

01:09:36.297 --> 01:09:37.298
Right.

01:09:38.091 --> 01:09:39.092
I said that.

01:09:39.175 --> 01:09:40.385
So, what's with you?

01:09:42.970 --> 01:09:45.223
Why are you so angry?

01:09:45.306 --> 01:09:46.766
[♪ gentle pop music playing]

01:09:47.809 --> 01:09:48.851
Well...

01:09:50.686 --> 01:09:52.522
Maybe it's because I like you.

01:09:55.483 --> 01:09:57.151
I don't like seeing you with another guy.

01:10:14.419 --> 01:10:15.878
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

01:10:42.363 --> 01:10:45.116
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:10:45.199 --> 01:10:47.285
[Kim Wooju] Does it bother you
that I like you?

01:10:47.994 --> 01:10:50.037
[Wooju] I think I really loved Meri.

01:10:50.121 --> 01:10:51.330
[Meri] Who is Miso?

01:10:51.414 --> 01:10:52.874
The name keeps popping up.

01:10:52.957 --> 01:10:54.125
She's someone you liked, right?

01:10:54.208 --> 01:10:56.711
[Jingyeong] He's the grandson
of Myungsoondang's CEO.

01:10:56.794 --> 01:11:00.089
Can't you just end it on your end, Meri?

01:11:00.173 --> 01:11:04.886
[Jingyeong drunkenly] Why doesn't
the guy I like see me as a woman?

01:11:05.261 --> 01:11:07.096
-[Kim Wooju] You got it wrong.
-[tires screech]

01:11:07.180 --> 01:11:08.514
I like Meri.

01:11:08.598 --> 01:11:11.601
[Youngsook] All is well as long as
Meri is cherished.

01:11:11.684 --> 01:11:13.144
[Kim Wooju] It's not because I'm sorry.

01:11:13.811 --> 01:11:15.021
It's because I like you.
